  "notes": "HIGH CONFIDENCE — primary-tier (WITS/UN Comtrade). India world total 2024: USD 142.99M across ~480,916 MT. Overwhelmingly a land-border/regional trade — Nepal alone is ~63% of value and ~65% of volume, with Bhutan and Sri Lanka next. That means maize content should target regional South Asian buyers and overland/short-sea logistics, NOT long-haul container buyers. Average unit value is low (~USD 297/MT), consistent with bulk feed-grade rather than specialty corn."
